A||||19||william_thorniii||DROPPED SPINDLES FOR THE MASSES!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||william_thorniii||03-08-2000||10:59 PM||||Gentlemen,<P>I am pleased to announce that Bell Tech drop spindles are now available for our 84-87 Fiero's through <A HREF="http://www.carparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.carparts.com</A>   With the various discounts available (misc. automotive magazines) you can get them for $159.10 before taxes.  <P>I knew there had to be a stockpile of these somewhere.  The only bad news is that they are ONLY available in 2" drop.  So what?  Well you MUST upgrade wheel size before these can be used.  <P>Have at it...<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||03-09-2000||12:06 AM||||Sure, now you tell us, after I already put in the lowering springs. Seriously though, if you're wanting a lower front end without the stiffer ride, this is the way to go.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Earne||03-09-2000||02:42 AM||||Thank you, william_thorniii!  Just placed the order for the BellTech drop spindles (2" front) and the BellTech rear lowering springs (1.5").  Shipping and all was $405.  Since I have 17" wheels, should be no problem.  <P>The only place I could find drop spindles these days is Rayne at:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/drop.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/drop.htm</A> <P>They were $594 and you had to use thier 12" brakes kit at $2,850.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/brake12.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/brake12.htm</A> <P>Let's see, $405 from BellTech for both ends or $3,444 from Rayne.  Thanks again, my brakes are fine, I sure don't need a $3,000 brake job.<p>[This message has been edited by Earne (edited 03-09-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||mshill||03-09-2000||12:28 PM||||So exactly what is the minimum wheel size required to use the BelTech 2 inch drop spindles.||||reg||5
Z||000004||william_thorniii||03-09-2000||12:55 PM||||mshill,<P>That depends on your vehicle and more specifically it's springs.  I would suggest checking your clearance between your wheel and control arm.  Based on that you should be able to figure out how much wheel you need to add after reducing that clearance 2".  I am planning on going to 17" wheels with custom offsets.. so this isn't a concern for me.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
Z||000005||Spyder||03-09-2000||01:12 PM||||Dropped spindles and lowering springs?<BR>This is for my kit car project.<BR>The front needs to be dropped 3”.<BR>I have 17” wheels.<BR>I have lowered it already with lowered springs and even cut those down, removed the rubber bump stop and it is bottoming out on hard bumps. <BR>What do you guys think?<p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 03-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfixit58||03-09-2000||01:29 PM||||William,<P>I just checked the price on carparts.com and the regular price for these spindles are $416. with the 1/3 off coupon it only brought the price down to $238. How did you get them down to $159? Can you share your secret??<P>Roy L.||||reg||8
