Z||000010||william_thorniii||03-09-2000||05:03 PM||||Gentlemen,<P>I regret to inform you that carparts.com is in fact out of dropped spindles.  I suspected that and called them prior to my order placement.  I was assured that if it was on the website, that they had it in stock.  I even ordered 2 sets knowing that they were in limited supply.  After all you never know how many Fiero's I will need spindles for in the future.  <P>O.K. so now that is blown, the way I see it is that we have 3 options.  1) Get on Street Dreams to get theirs to market.  Supposedly they have been working on it, but their first caster fell through.  I figure if a couple of us keep calling, we might be able to keep that fire under their hind quarters lit.  2) Get an example to be copied to someone.  I personally work for a CMM company so I could get them reverse engineered if need be.  Otherwise, the more traditional casting approach could be used.  Sure under this method, we would have to worry about patent infringement... 3) See if with enough support that we can get someone to start making these.  If we can't get a major player like Belltech in, then perhaps we could convince our own Mr. Dickman to look into the project.  I will check things out and see if I can find a set locally and use them as models.  That would lead to a CNC spindle.  They would be outrageous to produce but sure would look good.  <P>Who's with me... (mind you that anything will most likely be in the $300 range)<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
Z||000011||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||01:51 PM||||Friends,<P>Just got word from someone on the fiero-list that some sets of spindles were in stock and are arriving.  If anyone got in an extra order, or decided that they are not going to need them after all PLEASE look me up.  I spent some serious $ banking on the spindles and now will have a 88 GT rear suspension and stock front...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||8
Z||000012||Spyder||03-10-2000||04:03 PM||||This is from Street Dreams web site:Fiero drop spindles:<BR>These CNC machined cast steel spindles allow the front end of the Pontiac Fiero to be dropped a full two inches without sacrificing ride quality. This is designed for kit cars based on a Fiero, but it should also work well with unmodified Fiero cars. These drop spindles are the only ones we know to exist for this application.<BR>$295.00<BR> <A HREF="http://www.iserv.net/~strdream/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.iserv.net/~strdream/</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Phil||03-10-2000||04:48 PM||||A kitcar manufacturer that I know checked with Bel Tech and they said they would do another run of drop spindles if he would buy 100 sets. He said no.  I must have gotten the last set in existance a few months back because someone from the forum called  the place I got them from the next day and was told "All sold out". There is something to be said for living a good life.||||reg||1
Z||000014||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||07:05 PM||||Spyder,<P>I called Street Dreams earlier today.  They still do not know when their spindles will be available.  The story is that the original company they had lined up to do the casting was incapable of reproducing such a complex structure accurately and repeatedly.  So they are now working with a new company.  The CNC is fixtured and ready to run though.  When asked about a ballpark arrival date, none could be given.  It sounds to me like they still have a lot of work to do.  <P>This is the worst!  The problem for me is now I have a lot of parts that are on hold until I can get my hands on some spindles.  I have found a set that are for sale.  It just kills me to pay twice I paid for the same things on Monday.  This SUX!  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||11
Z||000015||Spyder||03-10-2000||07:14 PM||||William,<BR>I didn’t know if that was the same company or not, so I decided to post it any way.<BR>I think I would like a set myself, if they will work for me.<P>Anybody,<BR>What do you guys think, would it work to use the dropped spindles and lowering springs to achieve my 3 inch drop? <BR>Please note my post above. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||08:37 PM||||Spyder,<P>Anything is possible... ("I taught my dog to say I love you", Little Ceasars Pizza 1996).  The question is are you willing to do what it takes to get the job done. <P>I think that a 3" drop would be difficult period.  Truth is that those springs should drop you about 1.5" to start.  Then the spindles would add another 2".  So by these #'s you would have at least a 3.5" drop.  Since your lowering springs are cut, I would imagine that you would have at least a 4" drop.  Then the Fiero only has 6.3" ground clearance to begin with.  So that means no speed bumps for you.  You might need new lowering springs though.  At least in theory everything will work.  Although you will have a car that my butt would not enjoy riding in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Everyone,<P>Street Dreams told me that they would call me when they know an availability date.  I have called them several times.  I think that they are tired of hearing from me.  I will keep you informed when/if I hear anything.  <P><BR>William T. Thorn, III<P>  ||||reg||10
Z||000017||geyser||03-10-2000||11:11 PM||||Got my "no longer available" from carparts.com today, right after I received the confirmation. I placed my order right after it hit the post. WT3, thanks anyway for posting the info. ||||reg||9
Z||000018||william_thorniii||03-10-2000||11:59 PM||||Geyser,<P>I just wish I would have kept up with my fiero-list mailings.  I was out of town last week and got so far behind.  Otherwise I would have been able to let you all know on Thursday or Friday and I would now have 3 sets of spindles.  1 for my 86 and the others for ????  I can't believe how upset I am over this!<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||9
Z||000019||batboy||03-11-2000||01:45 AM||||Well boys, sounds like maybe you ought to consider front coil-overs as soon as you wipe all the tears away. Height is adjustable and you can install almost any spring rate.||||reg||1
